Task: Introduce a test runner (Phase 1, Tier 1 enabler)
Track: fy_tax_pack_20260729

SUMMARY
Installed Vitest 4.1.10 as a dev dependency and configured it for this repo.
No test framework previously existed; npm run build (tsc) was the sole gate.

FILES
- vitest.config.ts (new) - node environment, include tests/**/*.test.ts,
  "@" alias mirroring tsconfig.json paths
- tests/smoke.test.ts (new) - asserts alias resolution + pure-module import
- package.json - added "test": "vitest" and "test:run": "vitest run"
- package-lock.json - dependency tree
- conductor/tech-stack.md - new Testing section; Quality gates rewritten
- conductor/workflow.md - tier language updated; "no runner" accommodations
  removed where satisfied, retained for RLS/migrations which remain uncovered

WHY
Phase 1 introduces pure domain helpers (FY bounds, later Div 43) where an
error is expensive and a test is cheap. Deferring the runner would mean
shipping that math with no regression protection. The smoke test imports
through "@/*" deliberately: alias misconfiguration is the most likely
setup failure and produces confusing errors everywhere else.

VERIFICATION PERFORMED
- CI=true npm test  -> 1 file passed, 2 tests passed (153ms).
  Confirms runner works, alias resolves, and CI=true suppresses watch mode.
- npm run build     -> passed. Full route tree compiled, no type errors.
  Confirms tests/ and vitest.config.ts do not disturb the Next build.

